          957.0,
          1551.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "53d297266e8131915e7f99baa2482ce1ffcae705be65b87a6ad49e4ea6ec7207"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "2. If $\\mathbf{x} \\sim \\text{MVN}$, then any linear combination of the elements of $\\mathbf{x}$ is also $\\text{MVN}$. Specifically, if $\\mathbf{x} \\sim \\text{MVN}_n(\\boldsymbol{\\mu}, \\mathbf{V})$, a is a vector of constants, and $\\mathbf{A}$ is a matrix of constants, then",
