    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where the $ m \\times m $ and $ (n - m) \\times (n - m) $ matrices $ \\mathbf{V}_{\\mathbf{x}_1 \\mathbf{x}_1} $ and $ \\mathbf{V}_{\\mathbf{x}_2 \\mathbf{x}_2} $ are, respectively, the covariance matrices for $ \\mathbf{x}_1 $ and $ \\mathbf{x}_2 $, while the $ m \\times (n - m) $ matrix $ \\mathbf{V}_{\\mathbf{x}_1 \\mathbf{x}_2} $ is the matrix of covariances between the elements of $ \\mathbf{x}_1 $ and $ \\mathbf{x}_2 $. If we condition on $ \\mathbf{x}_2 $, the resulting conditional random variable $ \\mathbf{x}_1 | \\mathbf{x}_2 $ is MVN with $ (m \\times 1) $ mean vector",
      "source_page": 212,
